---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSecondary from '@/components/HeroSecondary.astro';
import { getLocalizedUrl } from '@/i18n/helpers';

const locale = 'en';
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/melafrit/ai-strategy';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal notice — publisher and host"
  description="Legal notice for the AI Strategy site: publisher, host, intellectual property, personal data, cookies, contact, applicable law."
>
  <HeroSecondary
    surtitle="Legal notice"
    title="Legal notice and privacy policy"
    lead="This page gathers the mandatory legal information (GDPR, French law) about the publisher, hosting, intellectual property and personal data of the site."
  >
    <span slot="stats">Last update: see CHANGELOG</span>
  </HeroSecondary>

  <article class="ai-container ai-prose ai-legal-page">
    <section>
      <h2>1. Site publisher</h2>
      <p>
        This site is published <strong>personally and independently</strong> by:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mohamed El Afrit</strong></li>
        <li>Independent educator, trainer and consultant</li>
        <li>For any official contact:
          <a href={`${githubUrl}/issues/new`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
            GitHub Issues
          </a>
          (official channel)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The site is not a commercial service, offers no transaction, and requires no registration
        to access its content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by <strong>OVH SAS</strong>, a French cloud computing company:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>OVH SAS · 2 rue Kellermann · 59100 Roubaix · France</li>
        <li>RCS Lille Métropole 424 761 419</li>
        <li>Phone: 1007</li>
        <li>Website: <a href="https://www.ovhcloud.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.ovhcloud.com</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        ⚠️ <em>The exact OVH hosting type (shared, VPS or Cloud) will be updated here once the
        decision is finalized. See the
        <a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/main/docs/architecture/skeleton-decisions.md`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">technical documentation</a>.</em>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>

      <h3>Source code</h3>
      <p>
        The entire source code of the site is published on the
        <a href={githubUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">public GitHub repository</a>
        under <strong>MIT license</strong>. See the
        <a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE-CODE`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LICENSE-CODE</a>
        file.
      </p>

      <h3>Pedagogical content</h3>
      <p>
        The entire pedagogical content (texts, handouts, diagrams, quizzes, glossary, capstone) is
        published under <strong>Creative Commons Attribution – NonCommercial – ShareAlike 4.0
        International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) license</strong>. See the
        <a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE-CONTENT`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LICENSE-CONTENT</a>
        file.
      </p>

      <h3>Third-party trademarks</h3>
      <p>
        The names of companies, organizations and institutions cited on the site (notably
        Massachusetts Institute of Technology, MIT Sloan School of Management, MIT CSAIL, as well
        as the organizations appearing in the case studies) are <strong>trademarks of their
        respective owners</strong>. Their citation on this site falls under <strong>nominative and
        descriptive use</strong> compliant with the French exception (article L. 713-3 of the
        Intellectual Property Code) and the doctrine of nominative <em>fair use</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is <strong>neither affiliated, validated, nor certified</strong> by MIT, MIT Sloan,
        or MIT CSAIL (see <a href={getLocalizedUrl('/methode/', locale)}>Method</a>, section 2).
        Any trademark used is cited for pedagogical reference purposes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Personal data and GDPR</h2>

      <h3>Principle: no collection by default</h3>
      <p>
        This site is designed to <strong>respect your privacy by default</strong>. Concretely:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No user account</strong> is created. No registration is required to access the content.</li>
        <li><strong>No tracking cookies</strong> are placed. No Google Analytics, no Facebook Pixel, no third-party audience measurement service.</li>
        <li><strong>No personal data</strong> is requested, collected or stored on the server side.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Local browser storage (quizzes)</h3>
      <p>
        The site's quizzes use the <strong>browser's localStorage</strong> to retain your progress
        and scores. This data:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Stays <strong>only in your browser</strong>, on your device.</li>
        <li>Is <strong>never transmitted</strong> to any server (neither ours nor a third party's).</li>
        <li>Can be <strong>cleared at any time</strong> via the "Reset my progress" button on the Quiz page, or via your browser settings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This means that if you switch browsers or devices, or use private browsing mode, your
        progress will not be preserved. This is an editorial choice to preserve simplicity and
        confidentiality.
      </p>

      <h3>Server logs</h3>
      <p>
        The host OVH may keep technical logs (HTTP logs) for security and diagnostic purposes, in
        accordance with French legal obligations. These logs typically contain: IP address, date
        and time of request, URL requested, HTTP code returned, browser type. They are kept for a
        limited period by OVH according to its own policy. See
        <a href="https://www.ovhcloud.com/en/personal-data-protection/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          OVH's data protection policy
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Your GDPR rights</h3>
      <p>
        In the absence of personal data collection on our server side, GDPR rights (access,
        rectification, erasure, portability, objection) do not give rise to any specific request
        to us. For host logs, address OVH directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. External links</h2>
      <p>
        The site contains links to external resources (institutional sites MIT, NIST, OECD,
        academic publications, communications from companies cited in case studies). These links
        are provided for pedagogical and sourcing purposes. We have no control over the content
        of these external sites and decline any responsibility regarding their content,
        availability, or their own privacy practices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The content of this site is provided for <strong>pedagogical and informational</strong>
        purposes. It does not constitute legal advice, financial advice, or strategic advice
        addressed to a specific organization. Decisions made by readers based on the content of
        this site are under their sole responsibility.
      </p>
      <p>
        Although the greatest rigor is applied to content production (see
        <a href={getLocalizedUrl('/methode/', locale)}>Method</a>), no guarantee of completeness
        or absence of error can be given. For any factual correction, open a
        <a href={`${githubUrl}/issues/new`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub issue</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Applicable law and jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        The site is published in France. This document is governed by French law. Any dispute
        relating to its interpretation or application falls under the jurisdiction of French
        courts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Updates to legal notice</h2>
      <p>
        The legal notice may be updated at any time. The current version can be consulted on this
        page. The history of modifications is traceable in the
        <a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CHANGELOG</a>
        and in the Git history of the repository.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ai-legal-page { padding-block: var(--ai-space-7) var(--ai-space-8); }
  .ai-legal-page section { margin-block: var(--ai-space-7); }
  .ai-legal-page section:first-of-type { margin-block-start: 0; }
</style>
